members.extended:
Output-side layers scale the output channels ($\ell$ is `(1, out, 1, 1)`);
feed-forward ones scale the input channels (`(1, in, 1, 1)`).  Merging multiplies the
filters, or each filter's input channels (per group for a grouped convolution).

methods.extended:
The new adapter is frozen and inactive, like any added adapter.  It
targets the union of the sources' modules (and feed-forward modules);
a layer one source does not reach sums the sources it has.
